### Rust template
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace ships the `tropism` and `tropism-mcp` binaries, and
# reproducible builds of a tool that analyzes other people's lockfiles are the least we
# can do. https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# insta writes these beside a snapshot on failure; review and accept, never commit.
**/*.snap.new

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# demo/swift is a real SwiftPM package, so an editor with SourceKit will resolve and
# build it if it is opened. The manifest and Package.resolved are committed; the
# 100MB of build output is not. The demos are analyzed by tropism, never built by us.
demo/swift/.build/
demo/**/.swiftpm/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/
